G2804.b:
⟪Κλαύδιος⟫, -ου, ὁ, ⟪Claudius⟫;
⟪1.⟫ the Emperor: ⟦Acts 11:28|Ac 11:28⟧ ⟦Acts 18:2|18:2⟧.
⟪2.⟫ A military tribune, ⟪C. Lysias⟫: ⟦Acts 23:26|Ac 23:26⟧.†

G2819.b:
⟪κλῆρος⟫, -ου, ὁ,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨נַחֲלָה⁩, ⁨גּוֹרָל⁩;] ⟪a lot⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ that which is cast or drawn: ⟦Matthew 27:35|Mt 27:35⟧, ⟦Mark 15:24|Mk 15:24⟧, ⟦Luke 23:34|Lk 23:34⟧, ⟦John 19:24|Jo 19:24⟧(LXX), ⟦Acts 1:26|Ac 1:26⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ that which is obtained by casting: ⟦Acts 1:17|Ac 1:17⟧ ⟦Acts 8:21|8:21⟧; of a part in the Kingdom of God (cf. Wi 5:5), ⟦Acts 26:18|Ac 26:18⟧, ⟦Colossians 1:12|Col 1:12⟧; pl. of the "cure" of a presbyter, ⟦1 Peter 5:3|I Pe 5:3⟧ (v. ICC, in l.).†

G2822.b:
⟪κλητός⟫, -ή, -όν
(< καλέω), [in LXX for ⁨קרא⁩, ⁨מִקְרָא⁩, ⟦Exodus 12:16|Ex 12:16⟧, al.;] ⟪called⟫, ⟪invited⟫ (as to a banquet, Æsch., ⟦1 Samuel 1:41|I Ki 1:41⟧, III Mac 5:14); in NT, always of the Divine call;
⟪(a)⟫ to some office: κ. ἀπόστολος, ⟦Romans 1:1|Ro 1:1⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:1|I Co 1:1⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ to salvation: ⟦Romans 8:28|Ro 8:28⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:24|I Co 1:24⟧, ⟦Jude 1:1|Ju 1⟧; κ. καὶ ἐκλεκτοὶ κ. πιστοί, ⟦Revelation 17:14|Re 17:14⟧; in gosp. (not in pl., v.s. καλέω) disting. fr.ἐκλεκτός, ⟦Matthew 20:16|Mt 20:16⟧ (WH, txt., R, omit), ⟦Matthew 22:14|22:14⟧; κ. Ἰησοῦ Χρ., ⟦Romans 1:6|Ro 1:6⟧; κ. ἅγιοι, ⟪saints by calling⟫, ⟦Romans 1:7|Ro 1:7⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:2|I Co 1:2⟧.†
